sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the 10.32 nm Chlamydomonas eyespot pigment stripe (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 of slot 3146. lambda(k_max) = 10.32 nm at a=0.07, b=0.95, Du=1, Dv=36. Finite-difference sweep Pearson r=0.99975, RMSE=0.200 nm. Linear stripe at the reference Dv is 10.259 nm (analytical 10.320 nm). Saturated stripe is 10.146 nm. Onset lambda(k_c)=6.986 nm. Isolated SEM cells: n=3, median equivalent diameter 4.72 um against a nominal 10 um vegetative cell. KS statistic of interior intensities 0.079. GIF 12 frames at 1024x1049. CV similarity to the Dartmouth SEM is 96.0. Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 83.7, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 530265 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd (sha256 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd), spec_fingerprint c41079d08516e24418edacb13a3820b8f31bff46de38d0a93c0cb0ebc5f205ac. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c41079d08516e24418edacb13a3820b8f31bff46de38d0a93c0cb0ebc5f205ac; artifact_sha256: 79b760e1b14cd10d4b6c6c87a239cc85a30b9290dd19deab4135c79cdc7c36fd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_turing_wavelength_s0/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_specimen.jpg=7f2a2df501eb7977...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor rate laws used here. | Foster and Smyth 1980: quarter-wave spacing d = lambda_light / (4 n), about 93 nm for 540 nm light at n=1.45, the successor scale. | Dieckmann 2003: carotenoid granules form the eyespot under the plasma membrane. | The Dartmouth SEM labels a 10 um scale bar. This pass measures 4.72 um bright-caps on three isolated cells.; reconstructed_in_script: k_c and k_max, with the unit chosen so lambda(k_max)=10.32 nm = 1.032e-8 m at age 0 Ma. | Dv sweep, Dv=Du negative control (sigma_max=-0.089), and ablation of u^2 v (sigma_max=-1.00). | Segmentation of the SEM and modulation of those cell bodies by the activator field.; transfer_boundary: At 10 nm the continuum limit is a modeling choice. Diffusion constants are scaled so the selected wavelength matches the assigned detail scale; they are not measured cytoplasmic diffusivities. | No fossil Chlamydomonas chronospecies is in this 1/1 series. The comparison is monomer 3.2 nm versus this stripe versus the quarter-wave spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published electron-micrograph measurement of exactly 10.32 nm. | Does not claim the SEM resolves that stripe. Orientation and radial spectra match because the frame keeps the real cell outlines. | Does not claim EYE2/EYE3 are dispensable. | Does not claim the 4.72 um bright-cap equals the 10 um nominal vegetative length.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Open limit, not a numeric gate: one assessor only, and the cell-diameter sample is three isolated bodies.",
            "remediation needed: R1 closed: isolated-cell window is 3-12 um; median 4.72 um on n=3, reference 10 um.",
            "remediation needed: R2 closed: CV terms recorded with the fitness result (orientation 0.965, radial FFT 1.000, coherency 0.914). Controls are scored.",
            "remediation needed: R3 closed: saturated wavelength 10.146 nm is reported beside the linear wavelength 10.259 nm." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.855"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second provider in this cloud loop)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
}

